### Page 3 of 44

```text
What is an Airport Master Plan?
“An airport master plan is a comprehensive study of an airport and usually describes
the short-, medium-, and long-term development plans to meet future aviation
demand.”
-FAA Advisory Circular 150/5070-6B Airport Master Plans
How often is an Airport Master Plan updated?
Updated roughly every 10 years, depending on the airport’s growth, changes in
aviation demand, and regulatory requirements.
-Last CYS master plan was completed in 2014
```

### Page 4 of 44

```text
What is the purpose of an Airport Master Plan?
+ A plan that . . .
▪Provides guidance for future
development
▪Satisfies future aviation demand
▪Is financially feasible
▪Identifies and responds to
environmental and socioeconomic
conditions
```

### Page 5 of 44

```text
What are the goals of an Airport Master Plan?
Prepare the airport for the future by
thoroughly understanding its
infrastructure requirements.
Maintain/enhance safe operations at
the Airport.
Foster stakeholder engagement through
open communication.
Develop a plan to optimize airport land
by maximizing the use of available
space.
Enhance the efficiency of operations of
the Airport.
Development program that promotes
fiscal sustainability.
```

### Page 6 of 44

```text
What do you get from an Airport Master Plan?
Airport Layout Plan
(illustrates the plan)
Working Papers/Final Report
(documents the why and how)
```

