Enplaned Passengers
Departures
2010-2011 Peak: American Airlines and Great Lakes Aviation services led
to a peak of over 20,000 annual enplaned passengers.
Post-2011 Decline: Termination of American Airlines’ service and reduced
flights from Great Lakes.
2019 Rebound: American Eagle launch of direct flights to Dallas/Fort
Worth led to a significant increase in passengers.
Pandemic Impact: COVID-19 and airport closures temporarily disrupted
services.
2021 Recovery: SkyWest resumed daily Denver flights, beginning recovery
of passengers.
2022 Recovery: Enplaned passengers recovered back to historical peak
levels.
2023 Decline: Runway renovations limited flight operations, leading to a
decrease in passengers.
2024 Projection: Recovery and growth, with passenger numbers
projected to reach 26,600 in 2024.
Source: USDOT T100 data, Dec 2024
```

