Task 05: Facility Requirements
Task Goal: Assess the ability of existing facilities at
CYS to accommodate the aviation demand
activity forecasts and identify when facility
additions and improvements may be needed
Key Subtasks:
+ Identify Planning Activity Levels (PALs)
+ Industry & Emerging Trends Analysis
+ Determine Appropriate Level of Service
+ Facility Requirements Analysis
```

### Page 22 of 44

```text
Planning Activity Levels
+ Managing Uncertainty: Planning activity levels (PALs) provide a flexible approach to addressing the inherent
uncertainty in long-range demand forecasting, allowing airports to adapt to actual activity levels rather than fixed
timelines
+ Trigger-Based Development: PALs help link facility expansions, such as terminal or fuel farm improvements, to
specific demand drivers like passenger growth or increased aircraft operations, ensuring projects are implemented
as needed
+ Strategic Capital Planning: By disassociating projects from specific years, PALs enable airport management to
adjust capital investments dynamically, accelerating or decelerating projects based on real-world demand trends
