### Page 30 of 44

```text
Taxiway Exit Analysis Planning Parameters
+ Evaluated the taxiway exits for Runway 09-27 to assess efficiency in aircraft movements
▪Runway Occupancy Time (ROT) is the duration an aircraft occupies the runway, measured from the moment it crosses the
runway threshold (on landing) to the point where it is completely clear of the runway. FAA aims for an average ROT of 50
seconds or less for arriving aircraft.
▪Taxiway utilization is a measure to determine if a taxiway is over or underutilized. Anything above a 75% is an overutilization
of a particular taxiway.
+ Tool used- REDIM (Virginia Tech)
▪Used for planning and designing high-speed runway exits, approved by FAA.
▪Includes a built-in aircraft database covering various Aircraft Approach Categories (AAC).
▪Calculates weighted average ROT based on user-defined aircraft mix.
▪Separate evaluations were run for arrivals on Runways 9R and 27L
+ Aircraft Fleet Mix for CYS
▪Derived primarily from existing Based Aircraft mix
▪~4%: CRJ series (assumed for commercial operations)
▪~13%: C-130 (assumed for military operations)Evaluated Runway 13-31 to determine compliance with FAA AC 150/5300-13B,
Change 1 Airport Design
```

